{"seconds": 46.1, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxc6, White plays Nxc6, and the queen is defended so White gains material. After all these checks, Ndc6+ is the key move that exploits the loose knight on d5 being attacked by the rook.\n\n**Best move:** Ndc6+\n\n**Main line:** Ndc6+ Bxc6 Rxd5+ (or after Nxc6 Rxd5 winning the knight with a material advantage)\n\n**Motif:** fork / discovered attack (the check forces Black to resolve it, and then the rook recaptures the knight)\n\n**Explanation (coaching note):**\nWhen the opponent's queen just moved to f6, look for moves that open lines for your rooks. After Ndc6+, Black must capture the knight. If Bxc6, then Rxd5+ wins the loose knight immediately\u2014the rook on d1 was defending it all along. If Nxc6, you still play Rxd5, winning material. Watch for moves that make your pieces work together.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ndc6+\", \"line\": [\"Ndc6+\", \"Bxc6\", \"Rxd5+\", \"Ke7\", \"Rxe5\", \"Qxe5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Ne6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Nxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "move": "Nf5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/4Nq2/n2nN3/5B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 b - - 5 16", "move": "Bxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2